<title>PAKISTAN: Karachi port handles 61,118 tonnes cargo.</title>
<headline>Karachi port handles 61,118 tonnes cargo.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1997-01-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pakistan's Karachi Port Trust said it had handled 61,118 tonnes of export and import cargo in 24 hours to 7 a.m. (0200 GMT) on Sunday compared to 34,077 tonnes in the same period on Saturday.</p>
<p>Cargo handling in tonnes:</p>
<p>				    Sunday	Jan 4</p>
<p>    Export cargo		11,344	13,988</p>
<p>    Import cargo		49,774	20,089</p>
<p>In the past 24 hours, three ships sailed and one berthed. In the next 24 hours, five ships are expected to sail and eight are expected to arrive.  </p>
<p>Berthing schedule of major vessels unloading or expected to unload at Karachi Port:</p>
<p>    Commodity	  Tonnes/TEUs  Ship		    Chilham</p>
<p>Castle 5/1 Fuel oil		 40,000	 Trade Resolve	7/1</p>
<p>Fertiliser	     24,657	 Danakos-1	    8/1</p>
<p>-- Karachi newsroom 9221-5685192</p>
</text>
